JUST IN: Tim Sheehy Urges GOP Holdouts to Back SAVE America Act as Trump Pushes Election Security

Tim Sheehy is calling on Republican holdouts to join President Donald Trump in pushing the SAVE America Act, arguing that election security measures enjoy overwhelming public support. Sheehy said Republicans have been unable to secure a single Democratic vote for proposals such as voter ID requirements, removing noncitizens from voter rolls, and strengthening mail-in voting safeguards. He said Trump is frustrated by Congress’s inability to advance the legislation and suggested that a small number of Republicans could help move the bill forward if they join the effort.


